Recurrent neural network language model (RNN-LM) and long short-term memory (LSTM-LM) language model is the state-of-the-art language method \cite{mikolov2010recurrent,mikolov2011extensions,bengio2006neural}. 
%The model structure of our document vectorization methods is based on the variants of RNN-LM and LSTM-LM. RNN-LM and LSTM-LM are chosen for our document vectorization for three reasons. Firstly, it can capture comparatively longer distance patterns in a document which are not restricted by the size of the context window. Thus, the model parameters of an RNN-LM can reflect the different grammar and style in the documents used to train it. Secondly, the hidden layer(s) of an RNN can provide a distributed representation of the input words so that the semantic and syntactic relationship among words can be captured by the model \cite{mikolov2010recurrent}. Finally, by controlling the size of the hidden layer, one may effectively limit the number of model parameters to be adapted for document vectorization.

