\item The strength of various bias components of our DV-LSTM were investigated. It is interesting to see that the LSTM bias vector $\b_m$ is outperformed by the class bias vector $\bc$. There are two possible reasons: (a) the abstract form of term frequency, which is represented by the class bias parameter, is still the most import feature baseline. (b) DV-LSTM used the Brown clustering method to organize its vocabulary class, which may offer better performance. Thus we also test the performance of the stand along Brown clustering term frequency feature in $c_{500}$ (the same 500 classes as the class bias vector in DV-LSTM), it shows that $c_{500}$ is still much inferior comparing to the 5-gram TF-IDF and $\bc$. Therefore, it could be inferred that it is the recurrent LSTM neural network structure and abstract feature extraction capability in the DV-LSTM makes the greater contribution to the performances. 


